      "The relevance of 'two goats': Pointing out that if no door opens, specifying 'two goats' is completely meaningless noise (Gricean Maxim of Relation). Why specify two goats unless the host needs two goats to guarantee revealing one?",
      "The binary action space: 'Offers me to change it' syntactically specifies a binary swap between two doors, which is mechanically incoherent if two doors remain unopened.",
      "Benchmark / Test-key reality: In automated evaluation or riddle keys, prompts like this are never coded as 'No (because the host forgot to open a door)'; they are universally keyed as 'Yes (2/3)'."
